 ## Background
-Voxel Point Sprite Rendering is an implementation technique found in open-source voxel rendering experiments. It is associated with the "OpenGL-Voxel-Splatting" project by sp4cerat [S4, unofficial] and the "voxel-renderer" by clayjohn [S3, unofficial]. These projects demonstrate the use of OpenGL point sprites and geometry shaders for efficient voxel visualization [S4, unofficial].
